/target
dist/
*.iso
*.img
*.raw
*.qcow2
*.tar.gz
/tools


# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Boot payload bundles are built artefacts, not sources (scripts/build-boot-payload.sh).
/assets/boot-assets/

# `CLAUDE.md` is tracked: the issue tracker cites it as the authority for
# constraints nothing else states, so a clone without it has dangling
# references. `AGENTS.md` stays local — it is a per-bench alias, not content.
/AGENTS.md

# The coverage backlog is the maintainer's working notes, not repository
# content. The issue tracker and the agent conventions are tracked instead:
# agents work one to a worktree, and a gitignored ticket is invisible to every
# checkout but the one that wrote it.
/docs/testing-backlog.md

# Agent tooling scratch space (worktrees, session state).
/.claude/
